@parnlogang I don't remember why I blocked you, but again, I must've had a very good reason, and I trust my past self more than my current self. I don't just block people for no reason.

You must've said or done something to piss me off, like constantly asking me to make or send you something, or you might've tried to scam me with one of those "I like your art, can I use it in a mural for a college project" messages. OR you could be a certain individual who I've had the displeasure of talking to on Discord who was a racist and a homophobe. (I deal with a lot of drama on a daily basis as you see, so I can't even remember who you are or why I blocked you.)

Regardless, I'm genuinely sorry, but whatever you did to make me block you in the past, learn from it and just move on with your life. I'm not taking any risks.

